    },
    {
      "box": [
        75.12000274658203,
        84.99369812011719,
        385.2574462890625,
        123.59259796142578
      ],
      "text": "C. mentioning a challenge faced by everyone.\nD. specifying a situation which makes us most anxious.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        136.5320587158203,
        464.3343200683594,
        175.43360900878906
      ],
      "text": "28. What point does the writer make about firefighters in the second\nparagraph?\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        176.43470764160156,
        510.3357849121094,
        215.03359985351562
      ],
      "text": "A. The regular changes of stress levels in their working lives make them ideal\nstudy subjects.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        216.1547088623047,
        471.6840515136719,
        254.8736114501953
      ],
      "text": "B. The strategies they use to handle stress are of particular interest to\nresearchers.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        255.8747100830078,
        523.3755493164062,
        314.3926086425781
      ],
      "text": "C. The stressful nature of their job is typical of many public service professions.\nD. Their personalities make them especially well-suited to working under\nstress.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        327.33203125,
        374.4205627441406,
        425.75360107421875
      ],
      "text": "29. What is the writer doing in the fourth paragraph?\nA. explaining their findings\nB. justifying their approach\nC. setting out their objectives\nD. describing their methodology\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        438.6920471191406,
        503.4547424316406,
        477.4736022949219
      ],
      "text": "30. In the seventh paragraph, the writer describes a mechanism in the brain\nwhich\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        75.12000274658203,
        478.59368896484375,
        480.1781921386719,
        557.0336303710938
      ],
      "text": "A. enables people to respond more quickly to stressful situations.\nB. results in increased ability to control our levels of anxiety.\nC. produces heightened sensitivity to indications of external threats.\nD. is activated when there is a need to communicate a sense of danger.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        603.6920166015625,
        169.10899353027344,
        623.1934204101562
      ],
      "text": "Questions 31–35\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        637.6520385742188,
        431.069091796875,
        657.1534423828125
      ],
      "text": "Complete each sentence with the correct ending, A–G, below.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        669.7537231445312,
        239.9373016357422,
        688.5526123046875
      ],
      "text": "A. made them feel optimistic.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        75.12000274658203,
        689.5537109375,
        460.0192565917969,
        767.9926147460938
      ],
      "text": "B. took relatively little notice of bad news.\nC. responded to negative and positive information in the same way.\nD. were feeling under stress.\nE. put them in a stressful situation.\n"
    }
